codemap 9
tour source-view
kind flow
author ai
group gui
note The file viewer, and where a human adds a range of lines as a step. Only the rows on screen become elements - a spacer stands in for everything above and below - which is what makes a four-thousand-line file scroll at the same cost as a short one. Each row is numbered, syntax coloured, and carries a coloured bar on the left where a step of the selected tour is anchored, green when current and red when stale. Comments on the file (comment-model) are drawn between the code lines, under the last line they are on, with their lines tinted orange (open) or green (answered); the code is drawn as one segment per stretch between comments, all scrolling sideways together. Clicking selects a line and pressing and dragging selects every line between, which the add button of the target strip below the toolbar, named for the selected lines, then turns into a step under the target the strip names (gui-authoring); double-clicking or ctrl-clicking an identifier jumps to its definition instead, and alt-clicking keeps it in the peek panel. The view only reads the Model: every click becomes an Action applied after the tree is built.

